34597 true] [17592186297954 1113 #uuid "3cbb4f71-8dff-56c2-b60d-738177511ef4" 13194139534597 true] [17592186297954 1145 "If $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nFrom the above equations, we can express $\\rho $, $\\theta $, and $ϕ$ in terms of $x$, $y$, and $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{y}{x},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\frac{z}{\\rho }\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $\\rho :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+2+49} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $(x,y)=(7,\\sqrt{2})$ lies in the first quadrant,  we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{7}) \\\\  & ≈0.199\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for $ϕ$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ϕ & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{z}{\\rho }) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{10}) \\\\  & ≈0.795.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the spherical coordinates of $S$ are $(10,0.199,0.795).$" 13194139534597 true] [17592186297955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297956 13194139534597 true] [17592186297955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297957 13194139534597 true] [17592186297955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297958 13194139534597 true] [17592186297955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297959 13194139534597 true] [17592186297955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297960 13194139534597 true] [17592186297955 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534597 true] [17592186297955 1041 "selection" 13194139534597 true] [17592186297955 1104 #edb/ref 17592186297958 13194139534597 true] [17592186297955 1110 #uuid "8ac891ce